hexagon: build the DSP library for v73 and v75

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The series did not link for v73 or v75. Eleven IEEE-typed HVX intrinsics
have no lowering on those cores without the compiler option -mhvx-ieee-fp
(vadd, vsub, vmpy of sf and hf, vabs hf, vfneg sf, vcvt sf to hf, the widening
vmpy of hf into sf and its accumulate form). Upstream keeps every use of them
behind __HVX_ARCH__ with a qf path. Our own kernels had two uses with no
guard, and this patch gives each the upstream helper that carries both paths:

- op_gdn_conv_step, gdn-conv-ops.c: Q6_Wsf_vmpy_VhfVhf by 1.0 widens f16 to
  f32. hvx_vec_f16_to_f32_shuff is the same instruction on v79 and the qf
  pair before it.
- hvx_silu_h_i16, hvx-silu-i16.h: Q6_Vhf_vabs_Vhf. hvx_vec_abs_f16 clears
  the sign bit, which is exact on every core.

On v79 the abs is now an and mask instead of vabs and the widen goes through
the inline helper, thus libggml-htp-v79.so is not byte for byte the same. The
two are exact equivalents: IEEE abs clears the sign bit, and the helper holds
the same widening multiply. test-backend-ops on the phone checks the two
paths, see the commit that carries this patch.

Why not the option -mhvx-ieee-fp, which makes those opcodes selectable on
v73 and v75 (found 2026-09-22): on hexagon-sim they are bit-exact, but on the
v79 silicon of the OnePlus 13 a v75 library that uses them executes with no
fault and gives inf on every f32 and f16 add, sub and mul (test-backend-ops:
ADD 76 of 76 cases ERR = inf, the same library passes REPEAT, CONCAT and
CPY, and the v79 library passes everything). No Qualcomm binary uses those
opcodes, and the v79 compiler lowers the IEEE intrinsics to the qf pair in
every mode. Thus the float path before v79 is qf, as upstream ships it, with
its known limits: one bit less than IEEE, no Inf, and the loss of relative
precision on a cancellation.

